          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "Grains of Paradise / Guinea grains: the capsules of Amomum meleguetta of West Africa (cf. cardamom), used as a spice and in medicine (OED s.v. grain n.1 4; Latham, Dictionary s.v. granum 4; Stieda, Venice 102). Latin granum paradisi. Not to be confused with the homonymous dyestuff kermes / scarlet grain (see granum)."
    }
